WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Attention on its own is permutation invariant. If you shuffle the input tokens, the set of outputs is the same, just shuffled.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:15.844
So we have to inject order. The original paper used sinusoidal positional encodings: sines and cosines of different frequencies added to the embeddings.

00:00:16.244 --> 00:00:21.188
Each dimension pair gets its own wavelength, from two pi up to ten thousand times two pi.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:27.866
Learned positional embeddings are the alternative: a second lookup table indexed by position instead of by token.

00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:35.766
Modern models mostly use rotary position embeddings, RoPE, which rotate the query and key vectors by an angle that depends on position.

00:00:36.166 --> 00:00:43.222
RoPE makes the dot product between a query and a key depend only on their relative distance, which helps length generalisation.
